{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming","id":1119620,"title":"Beast Analysis - Cross Gaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T13:28:39-07:00","id":1119620,"title":"Beast Analysis - Cross Gaming","content":"So having bought the premium hardcover VTR2 and BtP I've learned that.. Beasts talk a big game but they don't seem to really stand up to other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> At first glance, a Vampire's disciplines, access to blood sorcery, and even some coils (Zirnitra ._.) clearly outclass Beasts. What Beasts gain in freedom, they lose in raw power. Lair traits are largely -1 to 3 penalties or easily avoided damage (unless they stack beyond -5 , in which case you have a good chance against some supernaturals)<br /> Mages straight up look at something and it disappears, melts, or never existed in the first place, notwithstanding the incredible creative freedom they have with their powers.<br /> <br /> So I'm sitting here after having read BtP all weekend, what makes their claim to power have any meat to it? Especially since only Ugallu can clash an Obfuscated vampire, and other sort of lukewarm feelings I have about the birthrights. How should a Beast be played such that it's advantageous and indeed - even capable of defending itself against say a vampire who can just interrupt their movements or always go first. (Or in the case of Rhino's Hide and Flesh of Iron, has anywhere from 6-20 (with iron muscles) armour?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T14:40:06-07:00","id":1119634,"title":"","content":"Well in the more abstract Beasts do have the easiest time making friends with other splats.Not necessarily a huge combat advantage, but hey not terribly bad to have friends that might give someone pause before they consider attempted homicide. <br /> <br /> As for combat it's not like the Beghotten are propped up as the alpha predator species, so not unreasonable that they can claim to be dangerous even if they might not be able to take absolutely anything they come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T14:52:16-07:00","id":1119636,"title":"","content":"Attempting to kill the right specked beast is an exercise in futility almost akin to trying to do so with a Mummy. By that point, it can simply shadow the offender (literally) and destroy it at it's most convenient.<br /> <br /> Vampires turning to dust by the fiery dragon's breath, or mages having their souls cowered into a corner of the Primordial realm, and leaving them without any chance to cast anything comes to mind - so much that I'd use that as an explicit antagonist in a mage game akin to a Jack the Ripper figure.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the kind of power an apex can bring to bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:44:02-07:00","id":1119649,"title":"","content":"I tend to compared Beast to Changeling a lot in this regard. Both games are very flexible in what you can build your character to do, so how scary one is in any given type of conflict is exceedingly variable; whereas Vampire and Werewolf are much more focused in the kind of monster you're playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:05:45-07:00","id":1119658,"title":"","content":"Mistaking 'Powerful' for 'Interesting' here, I think.<br /> It doesn't matter where a Changeling, Kindred, Uratha, Arisen, Begotten, Awakened etc. stand on the powerscale, really. It is their relationship to Humans that mostly defines them, and with Beasts the additional fact they can get along with and insert themselves in the other splats' societies and survive. Purely for fluff and story reasons that makes them something different. I don't need to be able to beat the Gangrel Overlord mano a mano.<br /> <br /> What we all want is a good experience. I can have Mages and Uratha and Kindred in a Beast game that are impossible to beat, or only with a good strategy, or tricky, or easy, and vice versa. Whatever the game calls for, really. And when playing alongside each other, there should still be enough versatility with the Beast that it can do things others cannot. Especially in early games, Beasts start of strong and can support others well.<br /> Whiteroom comparisons are largely considered useless for a reason.<br /> <br /> You say Beasts have few powers? I think they are fine with their limitations and especially their variations: that Beasts' powers are situational is much of the charm for me.<br /> Are Kindred strong? Yes. But Kindred are basicallyexcluded from daylight hours, which can easily make certain stories I want to have not possible/need to be strongly reworked.<br /> Also, makes them very vulnerable half the time. Any Beast with something like Epic Direction Sense or Needs Must can easily devise a strategy to expose them to sunlight.<br /> Lair Traits are situational and hard to call down, sure, but they can be overpowered: A single starting Beast could wipe out all Kindred attending the Prince's court in one fell swope if they can call down intense flames or Blazing Light (a Minor Lair Trait).<br /> Those proposed character builds of yours take a certain amount of xp. Imo, a Beast will probably be a lot more versatile with this amount of xp, and still be a worthy opponent if done right. They have also nice mobility in being able to retreat into their Lair, wherein most chars are weaker than them.<br /> Also, don't forget that atm, Beasts have far more limited sources than other games: additionall material is sure to come.<br /> <br /> You do not have to like them, you would not be the only one to not like them, but to me, Beast is one of THE most interesting lines next to Promethean.<br /> And honestly, people would complain if they were dominating the others, too, wouldn't they? In fact, some already did with the level of power Beasts have, claiming they make &quot;other specialists obsolete&quot; or somesuch. (Was in an old post somewhere, not gonna search for that now)<br /> <br /> You want the King of All Monsters? Apex can be that. As can the Pack Alpha or the Prince/'s Sheriff.<br /> Are they unbeatable? No, they are not, as things that are per definition unbeatable are boring.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:36:05-07:00","id":1119696,"title":"","content":"Beast is certainly interesting, but the limits in place are pretty strong. ie: Ugallu's Birthright seem to be the main method of <i>any</i> beast to find <i>something</i> hidden, even supernaturals.Without their gift, you're hardly likely to expose someone long enough to mark them with Needs Must.<br /> <br /> It's interesting, but also frustrating to know you're not on equal footing without some serious extraneous set up which serves to close the gap.<br /> <br /> Also, Anakim and Ugallu seem to have by far the best Birthrights? a -2 penalty or -1 temporary Composure loss doesn't really compare to smashing Supernatural barriers and illusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 07-23-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:18:53-07:00","id":1119715,"title":"","content":"I'm running an offline Beast game---I'd have to say, in my experience at least, Beasts can be plenty powerful. In Conquering Heroes there's a Beast who <i>can summon sea storms</i>. If he wanted to do so, any coastal community he wants to destroy he can easily destroy. And places like NYC? While he couldn't take out New York, he <i>could</i> nevertheless wreak unholy amounts of damage to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:45:52-07:00","id":1119725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1119696#post1119696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is certainly interesting, but the limits in place are pretty strong. ie: Ugallu's Birthright seem to be the main method of <i>any</i> beast to find <i>something</i> hidden, even supernaturals.Without their gift, you're hardly likely to expose someone long enough to mark them with Needs Must.<br /> <br /> It's interesting, but also frustrating to know you're not on equal footing without some serious extraneous set up which serves to close the gap.<br /> <br /> Also, Anakim and Ugallu seem to have by far the best Birthrights? a -2 penalty or -1 temporary Composure loss doesn't really compare to smashing Supernatural barriers and illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I want to find something hidden, I just search for it the old fashioned way, or use a Nightmare on the owner of the Item to make him either paranoid about it and follow him, or make him think it wants to kill him with a curse, and offer to take it off of him.<br /> <br /> But I think you are right in that there is a certain lack of perception Atavisms, especially when it comes to things that are invisible.... I will homebrew one, thanks for the inspiration.<br /> <br /> I do not think this counts as a gap in power, though. Maybe an oversight, but maybe you have other examples of where you feel Beasts lack in power?<br /> Once more: With the right use of a nightmare, I can make people think their children are reptiles, my co-worker attack my boss so I get the job, the drug dealer rethink his life choices... Can other supernaturals do that? Yes they can! Is it the same? Absolutely not! And this difference can be worth playing the game.<br /> Maybe takea look at what Beasts are good at. Among those, we can count the ability to open any and all gateways, use people as back doors, and when it comes to AoE Damage, I think only mages and Titan Prometheans are capable of more output (might be wrong though, haven't read all books by far).<br /> <br /> <br /> That depends on your Chronicle. -2 to composure means the average person has basically no chance to resist. If the chronicle focuses on social maneuvers etc, it is actually more powerful/useful than the Anakim birthright of smashing barriers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T20:40:04-07:00","id":1119754,"title":"","content":"Also, something that came to mind:<br /> <br /> All Beasts can reflexively notice is someone around them is supernatural (except Demons because of that thing). Sure it doesn't allow them to break supernatural stealth powers, but it is resisted with Composure. Which means for just noticing other supernaturals in your Beast's area, a Composure penalty like that is actually very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:31:31-07:00","id":1119764,"title":"","content":"Has anyone played a Beast in a game of primarily one other gameline?<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem Arduras is having is because he's coming at them as antagonists, which they don't really seem to be made for except perhaps in a Demon or mortal game. They can do it. But as antagonists you really have to just go all out to make them tough, at which point you may as well go with anyone else. A vampire can't be active during the day but they can have ghoul operatives, and if you're running a cunning Beast with tentacles throughout the city and a wide variety of abilities, then you could do the same with a vampire. I think there's been a big push to have them as part of existing games, usually as allies. Even the Night Horrors book has very few playable Beasts as antagonists.<br /> <br /> I'm more curious about them alongside other games. The Atavisms themselves are pretty powerful, and pack a whole suite of abilities in one convenient purchase. But you can get by with just a few and raising your Lair seems to help most of them. Like, if I'm making a legendary werewolf Beast, I get Relentless Hunter for healing, Needs Must for hunting ability at the start, then maybe Limb from Limb during play. These are all directly impacted by Lair, with Needs Must's Perception bonus being Lair, Relentless Hunter's Toxin Resistance and Damage Lowering, and Limb from Limb adding Lair to damage. That's 3 or 4 Experiences and I've got my werewolf, done. All that's left is for them to be more powerful in terms of the abilities I've already mentioned. Sure, there's a lot of other ways to go about it but just for the legendary werewolf example, you're done. <br /> <br /> How has this kind of thing stacked up in games, specifically longer term ones, not one-shots, alongside a coterie of vampires or cabal of mages or krew of sin-eaters? Does anyone have any experience being part of a game like that and can speak to how advancement turned out? Or know of an Actual Play with this kind of setup?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:22:36-07:00","id":1119782,"title":"","content":"I think beast can be vary powerful sure they are not that good if you're going in guns blazing but a specialized beast can wreck shit up using the -2 compose power you can be great at mind control or with relentless hunter and unbreakable plus some merits you can get great armor plus more combos <br /> So yeah beast can be great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:44:46-07:00","id":1119787,"title":"","content":"If we must compare Vampires to Beasts, there is a metric to remember, a drum to beat in determining which is better:<br /> <br /> 1) Those who are clever about their advantages,<br /> 2) Those who are not.<br /> <br /> Beasts have all sorts of tools that can wreck merry hell on a vampire, and vampires have all sorts of tools that can wreck merry hell on Beasts. Depends on how you play it-but I will note a bias here and point out that Beasts <i>inherently</i> have a wider toolbox than vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T02:50:15-07:00","id":1119812,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Thank you for those two lines, I was searching for those when I wrote my long walls of wordiness!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> sadly, no, but if things pan out right, I might be able to tell you soon how a physical-defense-specced Beast might fare in Kindred Society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:28:57-07:00","id":1119998,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't any Beast with the Burning Lair Trait or the Dragonfire Atavism be utter murder against vampire?<br /> <br /> Also while I didn't play Beast I used as GM Beasts as antagonists for Mages and Mortals. To my surprise it's the Lair which is the biggest advantage of the intelligent Begotten, letting the Tilts cripple your opponents before swooping in is a winning situation<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:44:39-07:00","id":1120014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1119764#post1119764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone played a Beast in a game of primarily one other gameline?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't *primarily* another gameline, but it's a crossover chronicle. What I've noted playing a Beast is that my character is as powerful as I'm willing to push him. I can wreck shit up, but only if I'm willing to invest Satiety, which I might need the <i>next </i>time I need to wreck shit up. And because it's a very plot-centric story, finding time to feed is tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:49:03-07:00","id":1120018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1119787#post1119787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we must compare Vampires to Beasts, there is a metric to remember, a drum to beat in determining which is better:<br /> <br /> 1) Those who are clever about their advantages,<br /> 2) Those who are not.<br /> <br /> Beasts have all sorts of tools that can wreck merry hell on a vampire, and vampires have all sorts of tools that can wreck merry hell on Beasts. Depends on how you play it-but I will note a bias here and point out that Beasts <i>inherently</i> have a wider toolbox than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wider toolbox than the versatile Auspex, Dominate, Nightmare/Majesty and Physical Disciplines?<br /> A vampire with Celerity straight up trumps Beast in a stand up fight, the beast simply cannot keep up either perception wise (everything is a surprise attack for the vampire) or flat out can't do anything (first initiative uncontested, interrupts) and every power the vampire has is like that - controlling and versatile.<br /> <br /> Beast's nightmares seem cool but they don't scale to higher power games too well imo. Their atavisms look even cooler but are typically more limited in scope or raw power.<br /> The birth-rights are nice perks but a Satiety per attempt to pierce an Obfuscate that can just be immediately restored for 1/10-75 vitae is rough, to say nothing of actually trying to hit the kindred.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Werewolves and their gifts, I imagine.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm sure I'll have fun trying to play the underdog, the one who can only look in their direction and &quot;make friends&quot; short of bringing them into their Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:38:45-07:00","id":1120049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120018#post1120018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wider toolbox than the versatile Auspex, Dominate, Nightmare/Majesty and Physical Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally no Discipline or Devotion will let you generate sunlight, and learning powers outside your clan's Disciplines or the common five requires proprietary membership or becoming more vulnerable to another vampire's influence. Their greater abilities come at the price of precious Vitae or social leverage or territorial limitation. The active social/mental Disciplines all rely on a buildup of effects to be used at the higher levels, Auspex takes multiple scenes to use effectively and freely, Celerity's interrupt effect is both not free and not unlimited in use, and Obfuscate's interaction with surprise is wholly counteracted by simple dice bonuses.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, literally every Beast can develop any Lair Trait, Atavism, or Nightmare with the only real investment being legwork and time, and the associated vulnerabilities that <i>could</i> commonly come up are two-way and muted by the splat's incentives toward resilience in general. Beasts grow rapidly under pressure and synchronize well with other monsters, some of their supernatural powers are just <i>better versions of mundane Merits</i>, and their Atavisms include multiple sources of &quot;you just <i>know these things</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> A character that can regenerate health, have an innate Armor rating of 3, beat the Initiative of anyone who fails a surprise attack against them, know when their mind or perception is being altered, and/or unerringly track anyone they've ever made contact with <i>in addition to</i> potentially being able to summon disasters or breathe fire for free is inherently in a more flexible place than a similarly randomly-chosen vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:35:02-07:00","id":1120105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120049#post1120049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally no Discipline or Devotion will let you generate sunlight, and learning powers outside your clan's Disciplines or the common five requires proprietary membership or becoming more vulnerable to another vampire's influence. Their greater abilities come at the price of precious Vitae or social leverage or territorial limitation. The active social/mental Disciplines all rely on a buildup of effects to be used at the higher levels, Auspex takes multiple scenes to use effectively and freely, Celerity's interrupt effect is both not free and not unlimited in use, and Obfuscate's interaction with surprise is wholly counteracted by simple dice bonuses.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, literally every Beast can develop any Lair Trait, Atavism, or Nightmare with the only real investment being legwork and time, and the associated vulnerabilities that <i>could</i> commonly come up are two-way and muted by the splat's incentives toward resilience in general. Beasts grow rapidly under pressure and synchronize well with other monsters, some of their supernatural powers are just <i>better versions of mundane Merits</i>, and their Atavisms include multiple sources of &quot;you just <i>know these things</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> A character that can regenerate health, have an innate Armor rating of 3, beat the Initiative of anyone who fails a surprise attack against them, know when their mind or perception is being altered, and/or unerringly track anyone they've ever made contact with <i>in addition to</i> potentially being able to summon disasters or breathe fire for free is inherently in a more flexible place than a similarly randomly-chosen vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, in my Chronicle a vampire with the Camouflage devotion has fairly regularly dished out -30 to -40 to spot him, granted this is a high power campaign, but in a regular campaign -10 to -20 is still a huge buff lol. At any rate, a skilled user of Obfuscate would likely clash with an Ugallu, unless he was careless/spotted and got marked by another Beast with Needs Must.<br /> <br /> Likewise, they replaced the &quot;Beast&quot; requirements for those merits with &quot;Any Supernatural&quot; is that actually intended by the devs?<br /> I thought so, like it represented your natural born talent, realized upon your Devouring alongside your Hunger. A sort of fluffy built in power that isn't necessarily all that great (not like Epic Direction Sense can clash supernatural stealth) but still it's written as &quot;Beast&quot; not &quot;Supernatural&quot;.<br /> <br /> A fellow has said the Dev's meant to put them in every book, and so replace Beast with Supernatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 07-24-2017, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:25:40-07:00","id":1120124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120105#post1120105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, in my Chronicle a vampire with the Camouflage devotion has fairly regularly dished out -30 to -40 to spot him, granted this is a high power campaign, but in a regular campaign -10 to -20 is still a huge buff lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice modifiers in the double digits in general are outside the standard consideration for ChroD mechanics, so this is kind of a &quot;no duh&quot; situation if your definition of &quot;high power&quot; is &quot;dice modifiers literally several times the normal dicepool size.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At any rate, a skilled user of Obfuscate would likely clash with an Ugallu, unless he was careless/spotted and got marked by another Beast with Needs Must. </div> </div> </div>A skilled user of Obfuscate gains bonuses or applies penalties no larger than five dice to rolls relating to their passing unnoticed. Assuming a 1e bloodline Devotion carries over and stacks indefinitely isn't something that falls under consideration for how the games are designed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A sort of fluffy built in power that isn't necessarily all that great (not like Epic Direction Sense can clash supernatural stealth) but still it's written as &quot;Beast&quot; not &quot;Supernatural&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Epic Direction Sense is a supernatural power \u2014 it falls off with Slumbering \u2014 and therefore Clashes with the standard pool in cases where it would conflict with a stealth power. That's <i>the entire purpose of Clash rolls</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T18:14:41-07:00","id":1120172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120105#post1120105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sort of fluffy built in power that isn't necessarily all that great (not like Epic Direction Sense can clash supernatural stealth) but still it's written as &quot;Beast&quot; not &quot;Supernatural&quot;.<br /> <br /> A fellow has said the Dev's meant to put them in every book, and so replace Beast with Supernatural?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 112 says, &quot;If a Merit lists being 'Advanced' or 'Epic', it's a supernatural extension of a mundane Merit.&quot; That means the merits are supernatural powers and are eligible for clashing other supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> The reason those Merits say Beast is because they're meant to be accessible to Beasts. I think that Dev said they would prefer there to be merits like those for other supernatural creatures, but that doesn't mean that say, a werewolf should be able to take a Merit like the Advanced version of Eidetic Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T20:23:06-07:00","id":1120205,"title":"","content":"So here's a thing. What's dangerous about a vampire is not that she's fast or that she's unnaturally charming or that she can turn into a coyote. What makes a vampire dangerous is that she's <i>hungry</i>. All the powers, all the influence, all the elaborate social games... they're all just there so the vampire can cover her most basic need.<br /> <br /> And that's why so many other monsters get fucked over or fucked up by vampires. Because they don't get the desperation. They don't get the need. They don't get the <i>why</i>.<br /> <br /> But a Beast? A Beast <i>gets it</i>. A Beast knows what it's like to be hungry. A Beast knows you can turn hunger, the strongest motivation, into weakness. A Beast understands cutting off supports and starving the enemy.<br /> <br /> And the vampire knows the same thing.<br /> <br /> A face to face, tooth to neck, rotten breath in each other's faces kind of confrontation can be fun. But when Beasts and vampires clash, it's as two predators who understand each other at the very core. So they'll strike at the supports and the territory and all of the things around each other. And more often than not, rather than turn into two hungry animals circling each other, desperate for the kill... they'll have to strike a bargain. Because each knows the other, and knows how bad it'll get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:06:49-07:00","id":1120296,"title":"","content":"I was kinda hoping she'd confirm/deny the &quot;Any Supernatural can take a Beast specific merit&quot; but I like the idea of them being able to clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:09:09-07:00","id":1120298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120172#post1120172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason those Merits say Beast is because they're meant to be accessible to Beasts. I think that Dev said they would prefer there to be merits like those for other supernatural creatures, but that doesn't mean that say, a werewolf should be able to take a Merit like the Advanced version of Eidetic Memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of Scrolls would disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:12:26-07:00","id":1120301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120298#post1120298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Lodge of Scrolls would disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... werewolf lodge? only had 1 hit in the Idigam Chronicles book, a fluffy bit about someone named Nat Dory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:28:51-07:00","id":1120305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120301#post1120301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like... werewolf lodge? only had 1 hit in the Idigam Chronicles book, a fluffy bit about someone named Nat Dory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try Lodges: the Faithful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:50:04-07:00","id":1120326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120296#post1120296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was kinda hoping she'd confirm/deny the &quot;Any Supernatural can take a Beast specific merit&quot; but I like the idea of them being able to clash.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That same section I mentioned says that it's up to the Storyteller's discretion as to whether other Supernatural creatures can take Advanced and/or Epic Merits. Some of them seem appropriate for other Supernatural creatures, some don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:51:51-07:00","id":1120327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120298#post1120298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Lodge of Scrolls would disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems more like an exception, rather than a general rule. Lodges are not representive of Werewolves as a whole.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the book makes it clear that it's up to the Storytellers discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 07-25-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T10:20:14-07:00","id":1120392,"title":"","content":"Beasts are worse than what splat in what area, and at what EXP? Because the answer to who is better depends a lot on the circumstances, goal, and exp. Vampires are about control and bypassing systems by sending in their Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Challenge, get someone to do a thing</b><br /> <i>Mortal:</i> Fast-Talking, Sympathetic, and Pusher a Mortal can open 5 Doors on a single roll, which will be enough for all but the most stubborn of people. They also have access to Allies, Contacts, Mentor, and Status, which are amazing at getting people to do things. On defense, Etiquette 1 and Closed Book allow them to lie like a rug and have 10 Doors with 6 xp + A skill at 5. Mortals can stop incoming violence with that merit in Hurt Locker, even from frenzying creatures.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: </i><br /> Innately, Vampires gain the ability to Lash Out to achieve their goals, which nearly bypasses the social maneuvering system entirely for short term gain. They also gain Blood Bonds, allowing them to enslave others to their will. They also get the ability to ignore mental coercion by Frenzying.<br /> <br /> Social power beyond that is really exclusive to particular clans and covenants. Dominate 1-3 allows you issues commands and have them followed against someone's will, while also handling short term memories. Majesty 1-4 lets you enter ever more into someone's confidence and control their emotions. Nightmare 1-3 allows you to terrify people and give them Delusions. Auspex 1-4 allows you to glean more information from people which, while not directly applicable, can be used by a clever mind. The different Covenants have access to merits that make your social merits more efficient and/or more effective.<br /> <br /> <i>Werewolf:</i><br /> Innately, Werewolves gain Lunacy (forget the monster), Hunter's Mark (penalties that make prey easier to hunt), and a penalty against incoming mental powers while in a Frenzy.<br /> <br /> All werewolves can purchase Residential Area, which is a bit of an omni-merit and they gain access to a Totem, which can grant them exp-efficient benefits. They can gain perfect impression for a short term social gain with a gift. Some werewolves have access to additional dice on social rolls, generally up to +5. They have a couple more social gifts that grant conditions to people, and Half-Moons with high Honor can spawn social merits out of thin air. This doesn't include what they can do with spirits. They have several gifts related to gathering information. Half Moons can also bind magical oaths.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast:</i><br /> Alien Allure ensures good impressions, ensures people forgive you for your wrongdoing, grants a bonus to your social rolls, spawns Fame/Status dots out of thin air, and forces people to trust you and do you favors when you win a social contest -in addition- to the normal effects. Advanced Striking Looks is going to give you rote on Social Rolls. Mimir's Wisdom keeps you from being lied to. The Siren Atavism whose name I forget gives you yet more bonus social dice and makes you good at luring people, or attacking them with a sonic attack.<br /> <br /> Then you have Nightmares. Nightmares can control people (though not as well as Dominate), they can instill strange beliefs in people, or otherwise manipulate them to do what you want so long as you can contextualize it as being motivated by horror/trauma. With Mummy Kinship (and probably Ventrue Kinship) you can even alter memories. This i on top of their innate ability to start with a Good Impression with all supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <i>Conclusion:</i><br /> (Kindred = Beast) &gt; Werewolf &gt; Mortal is how I see it, but note that all of those can reach the point of &quot;one roll = you do a thing,&quot; and have a good chance of passing that roll. Kindred pull ahead because of their ability to have long term gains to their powerbase through their powers, while Beasts have some fringe benefits (immunity to lying, autoforgiveness) that really stand out. Both can affect memories. Notably, each is best in their own way...<br /> - Kindred is best at aquiring and exorcising control<br /> - Werewolf is good at setting up the hunt.<br /> - Beast is good at being an abuser and breaking people down until they do what you want, while they welcome you with open arms because it'll totally be different this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T15:45:46-07:00","id":1120528,"title":"","content":"How much exp are your characters getting in this game? If you want a challenging encounter you should look into Incarnates. It's pretty easy to make one with 45 health, 13+ armor, and the ability to completely heal all lethal every round. And 10 automatic successes on stealth rolls. Also intimidation rolls. And a +40 lethal kraken grapple combo that hits everyone within 60 feet. All that takes less than 100 exp, including the 45 just to get to Lair 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T16:17:44-07:00","id":1120532,"title":"","content":"Well, currently I'm playing Jack. A Gangrel with 5 in Protean, Animalism, Obfuscate, Celerity, Vigour, Praestantia, Resilience. He can at will make 20 armour, or J's Gait.<br /> With Threnodies and devotions he's a real Monster's Monster. Dude has proven time and time again to be just damn near unkillable (Wyrm 5, Ascendant 3) and just all around nasty.<br /> <br /> Dude hits you he gets a grapple, gg you just took upwards of 20 aggravated and if that didn't kill you your stunned or unconscious for twice as many turns, that's assuming he's nice enough to let you see him, not just using Obfuscate/Celerity/Camouflage (Devotion) to just snap you out of the dark. Also, Celerity is free surprise attacks for hours with Forced March and things like Guardian Vigil flat out negate attempts to surprise you.<br /> <br /> Basically, I make combat characters, Vampires seem to own that category, then Demons, Werewolves, then Beast, only because I don't know enough about Promethean, Geist, etc.<br /> When a vampire can flat out negate several game mechanics (Surprise, and also good luck finding them or even <i>touching</i> them with their ~40 defense.)<br /> <br /> We might be re-rolling new characters though, since this game has clearly gone well above what the devs designed and everything is a contested action or calsh of wills of rather epic proportions. We outclass princes and methuselah by orders of magnitude as they're written in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T17:17:24-07:00","id":1120553,"title":"","content":"When you have (nearly) unlimited exp, sure, vampires have a ton of supplements to draw from and can get incredibly broken. But I'm also counting what, over 130 exp in those disciplines alone, never mind BP, Devotions, Merits, Attributes, Skills. As befits their theoretically infinite lifespans vampires have an insane amount of crazy powers they can learn but those powers are super expensive and most characters are only going to have mastered a small handful, if that.<br /> <br /> Splats aren't intended to be balanced anyway, but if you're looking to get a rough sense of how well they compete in a given field you really need to compare at few benchmarks. 0, 25, 50, 100, exp, compare a few sample characters with equal amounts. Vampires can go deeper in a lot of areas but Beasts can go a lot wider a lot faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T17:35:10-07:00","id":1120558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120532#post1120532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, currently I'm playing Jack. A Gangrel with 5 in Protean, Animalism, Obfuscate, Celerity, Vigour, Praestantia, Resilience. He can at will make 20 armour, or J's Gait.<br /> With Threnodies and devotions he's a real Monster's Monster. Dude has proven time and time again to be just damn near unkillable (Wyrm 5, Ascendant 3) and just all around nasty.<br /> <br /> Dude hits you he gets a grapple, gg you just took upwards of 20 aggravated and if that didn't kill you your stunned or unconscious for twice as many turns, that's assuming he's nice enough to let you see him, not just using Obfuscate/Celerity/Camouflage (Devotion) to just snap you out of the dark. Also, Celerity is free surprise attacks for hours with Forced March and things like Guardian Vigil flat out negate attempts to surprise you.<br /> <br /> Basically, I make combat characters, Vampires seem to own that category, then Demons, Werewolves, then Beast, only because I don't know enough about Promethean, Geist, etc.<br /> When a vampire can flat out negate several game mechanics (Surprise, and also good luck finding them or even <i>touching</i> them with their ~40 defense.)<br /> <br /> We might be re-rolling new characters though, since this game has clearly gone well above what the devs designed and everything is a contested action or calsh of wills of rather epic proportions. We outclass princes and methuselah by orders of magnitude as they're written in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not sure about your hierarchy. A Demon, at least, could ping them with nearly automatic Aggravated Damage every round and potentially supercede their initiative once they get a hit in (Victory At Any Price, Hellfire, Fast Attack, though they may also need Wound Healing to keep up with the damage Victory At Any Price inflicts), and make them fail their Stealth by giving themselves away (Marco Polo, among other Embeds). Turn Blade and Just Bruised can also reduce your 20 Aggravated damage... to 1 Bashing Damage, if that. Many of these options are available to starting or early Demons. And that's not even getting into Show of Power shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-25-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:15:36-07:00","id":1120718,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a> Those numbers are WAAAY out there. I agree that your game has left the boundaries of a normal game long ago xD<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Beasts start out quite strongly, and most of their Atavisms scale well, but they mostly grow in Versatility with time. Due to the Low/Normal/High Satiety mechanics in Atavisms and Nightmares, they also have quite a situational character that waxes and wanes in what they can do. Some like it, like I do, others don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":