 wills of rather epic proportions. We outclass princes and methuselah by orders of magnitude as they're written in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd like to know how your character got mastery over all those disciplines without becoming the mind fucked slave of not 1 but several elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:00:03-07:00","id":1120731,"title":"","content":"Probably diablerie. Can't be the slave of someone who's dead, and once you've learned the first dot you should be able to figure the rest out by yourself. Besides, a single sip can at most create a first stage blood bond (except through the Coil of the Voivode or some kind of blood sorcery) which is nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:04:33-07:00","id":1120733,"title":"","content":"Praestantia was a gift from a vampire in the group that somehow has &gt;3 bloodline disciplines. (Abjurism, Obtenebration, Sunnikuse, the En gifts, and Cadavera - corpse manipulating)<br /> Things like THAT are why half the party is like &quot;wtf&quot; and why I'm sitting here going &quot;I couldn't make a Beast that could stand with this party.&quot; lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 07-26-2017, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:34:04-07:00","id":1120770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120733#post1120733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praestantia was a gift from a vampire in the group that somehow has &gt;3 bloodline disciplines. (Abjurism, Obtenebration, Sunnikuse, the En gifts, and Cadavera - corpse manipulating)<br /> Things like THAT are why half the party is like &quot;wtf&quot; and why I'm sitting here going &quot;I couldn't make a Beast that could stand with this party.&quot; lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of sounds like something your table needs to work out... Because the scope of your game seems far beyond what the core book of Beast has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:38:28-07:00","id":1120771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120733#post1120733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praestantia was a gift from a vampire in the group that somehow has &gt;3 bloodline disciplines. (Abjurism, Obtenebration, Sunnikuse, the En gifts, and Cadavera - corpse manipulating)<br /> Things like THAT are why half the party is like &amp;quot;wtf&amp;quot; and why I'm sitting here going &amp;quot;I couldn't make a Beast that could stand with this party.&amp;quot; lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>At those levels, roll up an Incarnate. They have vague, ST defined powers as part of their set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:06:45-07:00","id":1120779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120771#post1120771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At those levels, roll up an Incarnate. They have vague, ST defined powers as part of their set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. To play on the level of legendary vampires, you need to play a legendary Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:14:50-07:00","id":1120783,"title":"","content":"Question about the Beast, because arbitrarily upgrading to an Incarnate is not my taste(if I throw an Incarnate at you, the earth had better buckle beneath and the sky shatter):<br /> <br /> Are you throwing the Beast alone at this group, and if so, why? Also, what exactly are the tactics you're trying with the Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:17:06-07:00","id":1120786,"title":"","content":"An Incarnate can have nice little abilities like only taking damage of any kind by Anathema. So to damage him, you first need to find a Hero that is able to stand up to him long enough to place one on him, hoping that he even is in a state where one can be placed on him.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I agree with the others: If you want a game on THAT level, spend 120 Xp on the Beast and make it an Incarnate. That'll do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:10:22-07:00","id":1120844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120786#post1120786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Incarnate can have nice little abilities like only taking damage of any kind by Anathema. So to damage him, you first need to find a Hero that is able to stand up to him long enough to place one on him, hoping that he even is in a state where one can be placed on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more complicated than that. What you said is partially supported by:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial p.243</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Impenetrable Skin:</b> The Beast gains armor equal to her Lair dots against all attacks not from her Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's an universal feature of Incarnates that changes that picture:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial p.244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>No More Heroes:</b> Heroes might still seek the Beast out, but they cannot place Anathema on her and the Hero\u2019s power of Heroic Tracking is of no use. The Beast Incarnate can remove the Hero\u2019s gifts, granting him clarity and showing him exactly who he is in the scheme of things \u2014 an interloper, an intruder in a story that was never his.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding a Hero is pointless unless you've destabilised the Myth, and at that point a Hero is unnecessary, as seen here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial p.244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Destabilization:</b> The Legend can\u2019t live forever, at least not unchanged. The Incarnate Beast must keep ironclad control over its own Myth, or else abandon it and its power. If something happens that destabilizes such a Beast\u2019s Myth, the Beast loses the powers associated with its Inheritance and gains a significant weakness: Anyone, whether Beast, Hero, human or otherwise, can place Anathema on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:17:29-07:00","id":1120847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120733#post1120733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things like THAT are why half the party is like &quot;wtf&quot; and why I'm sitting here going &quot;I couldn't make a Beast that could stand with this party.&quot; lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it seems hard to escape the fact that some of this comes down to your group having made/accepted house rules that make vampires more powerful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:30:29-07:00","id":1120857,"title":"","content":"Tactics? Eshmaki or Ugallu are the only two that stands a chance, dragon fire and from the shadows or shadowed soul. Needs must for tracking. Ugallu burns their satiety spotting or Eshmaki gets the jump, maybe. But yea, we'll have to sit down with the guts of our game because I haven't even gotten to the two vampires that are really the vampire with a ton of bloodlines in oath of matrimony to a moros mage. Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:51:47-07:00","id":1120900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120857#post1120857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tactics? Eshmaki or Ugallu are the only two that stands a chance, dragon fire and from the shadows or shadowed soul. Needs must for tracking. Ugallu burns their satiety spotting or Eshmaki gets the jump, maybe. But yea, we'll have to sit down with the guts of our game because I haven't even gotten to the two vampires that are really the vampire with a ton of bloodlines in oath of matrimony to a moros mage. Lol</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you fight an armored drake that lurks in a lake of acid in a chamber that shatters weapons when they're used? <br /> <br /> What will a vampire do if the drake grabs them and pulls them under?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:55:22-07:00","id":1120933,"title":"","content":"Tactics matter, because no one is going to go in and just blindly swing a punch, and because of this, you'll excuse me if I don't quite buy that <i>only</i> an Eshmaki or Ugallu can challenge them.<br /> <br /> I mean, mind you, your PC's are powerful enough you should consider ending the campaign and going onto something else, but if we must challenge them, then the assumptions are wrong.<br /> <br /> 1st problem! I saw no mention about what else a Beast is bringing to the game, in terms of allies. Considering that Beasts are crossover characters and that one of the two universal toolkits that every Beast is basically grabbing allies in the other corners of the world and empowering that, that seems like a phenomenally stupid thing to do. What good is Obfuscate and Celerity against spirits of stealth who can simply see you by virtue of trying to <i>hide</i>? How useful is all that armor and defense from Protean, Resilience, and Celerity if a Fae or Strix can just declare you're vulnerable and you can't do shit about it? In an entire franchise where no one stands alone, a Beast <i>absolutely does not stand alone</i>.<br /> <br /> 2nd problem! So your players have impressive dice pools and applied modifiers.<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to power through them then? Don't set them on fire, set the building on fire and drop lair traits that trap them on the place. They can stand against a truck, but can they stop an entire ocean? THey can't, so get creative and sweep them to the bottom of the ocean-it's not that hard for a Beast create that sort of flow. There are plenty of options in the Chronicles world that just <i>happen</i>, and a Beast is one of the best character types to go, hunt down these options, and bring them to bear. Lair allows them to dictate the flow and direction of the environment in a way that makes werewolves drool and make even elder vampires sweat.<br /> <br /> Like, with just the basic power options of a Beast and some creative thinking, you can easily panic any of your players. Nevermind some of the really creative uses of Birthrights, Atavisms, and Nightmares.<br /> <br /> If you really wanna take someone &quot;underpowered&quot; and challenge someone absurdly powerful, stop and sincerely think about how you'd go about it as a player character. Good players are creative and can overcome any challenge with a good enough plan. On top of that, players with characters that big (like yours) tend to overtly rely on just their powers, so it's not that hard to start spiralling around them.<br /> <br /> Be smart, stack the deck with your resources, hit them hard and without mercy. The only additional principle you need as a GM is to remember to give them a chance.<br /> <br /> And, seriously, if you can't imagine a challenge for your PC's, it's time to end the game. Sometimes, you just have to accept you've arrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:12:48-07:00","id":1120940,"title":"","content":"We're at the point that there are no unaccepted consequences. If one of the players doesn't like he he goes and rewrites history so it never happened. Hoping to re-roll baseline characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:36:34-07:00","id":1120960,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a> wow. Boy, that sounds.... boring.<br /> I mean, playing an op char like that can be fun - for like, 2 sessions? When there is no challenge, there is no game. There is just the narrative of Kirito or Ainz Ool Gown: OP Character that always wins. Also, how long did it take you to get there?<br /> You can still take care of characters like that. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> already explained, it just takes proper planning and an honest chance. And taking similar resources into Account, a Beast could do funny things like lure your vamp to fairy, then escape into the primordeal dream himself while leaving you stranded. Don't have to fight you if you cannot go back. He could get the vamps into his Lair full of Fire and Sunlight (very appropriate for a Surtr type of character). A dead character cannot reroll. They can be beaten. Hard to do, yes, but possible.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'd make a new char. You'll enjoy that much much more.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> Oh, I misremembered Impenetrable Skin. Thanks for the clear-up!<br /> So yeah, even an Incarnate can be dealt with. It's just super-hard (which makes it super-fun!).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:39:31-07:00","id":1120966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1120940#post1120940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're at the point that there are no unaccepted consequences. If one of the players doesn't like he he goes and rewrites history so it never happened. Hoping to re-roll baseline characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it floats your boat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:47:31-07:00","id":1120970,"title":"","content":"Lol, two started that powerful, through gnashing of teeth and several chronicles the other two lessened the gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:59:33-07:00","id":1121066,"title":"","content":"Hm. Not my type of playing, but as long as you enjoy it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:14:22-07:00","id":1121073,"title":"","content":"Still talking pure numbers for a bit, Siren's Treacherous Song ignores both defense and most forms of armor when the Beast spends Satiety, The Kraken Grab (Monster From the Deep that is) ignores defense, and Eye of Heaven can potentially surprise even characters normally immune to surprise. (I mean in general supernatural stealth is supposed to get a clash of wills against supernatural alertness). At most levels of exp any one of those atatvisms can ruin somebody's day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:21:42-07:00","id":1121075,"title":"","content":"Would you rule that Siren's Treacherous Song, after it deafens you, is unable to hurt you again? At least until one stops being Deaf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-26-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:45:29-07:00","id":1121088,"title":"","content":"Can still hurt you, I'd say. The pressure doesn't lessen just because you cannot hear it anymore. Deafen is just bonus-damage.<br /> <br /> If you couldn't destroy items like glass with it, I would say it's a sensory attack, but from the way it is written, it really isn't. Even a deaf person would suffer blood vessels ripping etc. from the scream.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T17:50:33-07:00","id":1121111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1121088#post1121088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can still hurt you, I'd say. The pressure doesn't lessen just because you cannot hear it anymore. Deafen is just bonus-damage.<br /> <br /> If you couldn't destroy items like glass with it, I would say it's a sensory attack, but from the way it is written, it really isn't. Even a deaf person would suffer blood vessels ripping etc. from the scream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? But it even says it only ignores armor and magical protections unless they defend your senses. 'This attack ignores armor and any form of supernatural protection that does not shield the victim\u2019s senses.' Why bother having ear protection work if being deaf doesn't protect you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T18:07:16-07:00","id":1121113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1121111#post1121111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? But it even says it only ignores armor and magical protections unless they defend your senses. 'This attack ignores armor and any form of supernatural protection that does not shield the victim\u2019s senses.' Why bother having ear protection work if being deaf doesn't protect you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Well, I suppose we should just ignore some physics and go with the 'glass breaks for fluff reasons' route.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the &quot;Nightmare's are unusuable against other supernaturals&quot; matter, I want to point towards the Kinship Nightmare You are Infected High Satiety Effect: -4 Dice pool, but no resistance applied. Much fun can be had, especially since at this point, it also works as a contact drug, and even trace amounts are enough to have people suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T20:06:13-07:00","id":1121162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1121113#post1121113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. Well, I suppose we should just ignore some physics and go with the 'glass breaks for fluff reasons' route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe sound breaking glass has more to do with the particular frequency of the sound, rather than the volume of it. A singer can break a glass with their voice without rupturing people's eardrums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T02:15:19-07:00","id":1121230,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> <i>A </i>glass, perhaps, but not all glass in the area, which would not only swing at different frequencies, but also be vastly different in how much energy it takes to break them: just hitting the frequency is by no means enough. You need something like 105 Dezibel just to break a wine glass. Simple tumbler would be vastly more sturdy. A window far beyond that. If car glass breaks, that is approximately 163 db. 140 db is the point of definite long-term damage for all frequencies, and the threshold of pain, and causing your throat and vocal chords to resonate. At 145 db, vision is affected, at 150 joints are affected and swallowing become hard, 165 is similar to the internal pressure of a jet turbine, at around 170 db it is about 1 pound of force per square inch. 180 db finally would equal the force of 1 pound of TNT exploding at 15 ft distance. 190 is where eardrums rupture, 200 db is enough to cause death from the sonic shockwave alone.<br /> <br /> With such a voice, you could definetly do more than inflict a simple tilt. You could cause mini-explosions.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think we're not meant to take this so physically acurate.<br /> <br /> If you do, you should probably assume 165 db, which is enough to shatter most glass, and the other effects (percieved cooling of the air, balloons exploding, flashlights dimming and brightening according to frequency, and being about as loud as a Boeing 747 at take off in general) aren't overwhelming.<br /> Also, keep in mind that the dB is an exponential scale, adding 10 to the value about equals doubling the sound's force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-27-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:58:51-07:00","id":1122045,"title":"","content":"So lets see...<br /> <br /> Social Beast<br /> Atavisms: Alien Allure; ???<br /> Nightmares: You Must Obey; ???<br /> Merits: Striking Looks 2, Advanced Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic 2, Fast-Talking 4<br /> <br /> Investigative / Tracking Beast<br /> Atavisms: Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must<br /> Nightmares: You Deserve This; ???<br /> Merits: Advanced Eidetic Memory 1, Direction Sense 1, Advanced Direction Sense 2, Epic Direction Sense 2, Eye for the Strange 2, ??? 2<br /> <br /> Infiltration Beast<br /> Atavisms: From the Shadows; Shadowed Soul<br /> Nightmares: You Are Not Alone; ???<br /> Merits: Close-Quarters Fighting 4, ??? 6<br /> <br /> Combat Beast<br /> ....<br /> Okay, so real talk for a minute. Literally any Beast with a damaging environmental tilt and an easily accessible tilt wins against anything not immune. You get Behold, My True Form! To help round out any of the other concepts with combat, particularly with other metaNightmares.<br /> <br /> Shadowed Soul + Behold, My True Form! / Siren's Song lets you attack from relative safety.<br /> <br /> Infested + Fist of Nightmares lets you do a lot of damage to people. Throw in Basilisk's Touch for added goodness.<br /> <br /> Looming Presence + A Good Intimidation Roll will let you one shot most people.<br /> <br /> Cyclopean Strength makes your strength based attacks automatically hit. Combine with the above.<br /> <br /> Epic Iron Skin + Unbreakable makes for a nearly unkillable juggernaut.<br /> <br /> Killer Instinct 3 + Advanced Killer Instinct 1 is a nice damaging add on.<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter + Unbreakable + Epic Iron Skin 5 + Killer Instinct 3 + Advanced Killer Instinct 1 can handle anything.<br /> <br /> Just so many options for Combat, and none of them terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:40:36-07:00","id":1122057,"title":"","content":"Compare.<br /> <br /> Social Vampire<br /> Disciplines: Dominate 3 or Majesty 3<br /> Merits: Honestly doesn't matter. Allies, Contacts, Resources, Status to taste.<br /> <br /> Compare:<br /> Dominate Vamp can get someone to perform simple tasks with a aingle roll and alter memories within a scene. With more effort, they can implant commands.<br /> <br /> Majesty makes people want to do the Kindred Favors and allows the Kindred to swing their emotions all over the place.<br /> <br /> Beasts can get a target to perform any task, even long term ones in a single roll *and* get them to be semi-complicent. At low Saity they give the Charned Condition in addition to their normal effects. You Must Obey is the stopgap for the immediate control, although it has more holes than Dominate. Tabula Rasa can match or exceed Dominate's memory wiping powers, bit not altering. <br /> <br /> Overall, the Beast seems like a very inbetween the two Kindred Builds. It isn't going to be as reliable as either of the two Kindred Builds at their thing, but it can do a bit of everything. Kindred are going to have more merits to throw at support structures. A Beast *can* match it, but in that case they want to really focus on improving their dicepool so they can reliably Force Doors.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would be happy with any of these Social Characters on my team. Remember that a Beast, in addition to performing these duties, also<br /> - Can open portals to places<br /> - Autodetect the supernatural<br /> - Empower other splat's abilities<br /> - Drop their Lair on people which, as discussed, lets them Win Combat agaonst most things.<br /> <br /> Investigation / Tracking Vampire<br /> Disciplines: Auspex 3<br /> Merits: Acute Senses 1, Bloodhound 2, Cacaphony Savvy 3, Distinguished Pallet 1, Dream Visions 1, ??? 2<br /> <br /> Comparison:<br /> Kindred can learn a lot about their surroundings and people's weaknesses using Auspex. Auspex 3 scans a location. All useful. They gain some serious bonuses tracking and identifying things by blood. Cacaphony Savvy keeps the Kindred in the know about the city's going ons. If you can swing Where the Bodies Are Buried you can get even more information. Dream Visions optional.<br /> <br /> Compare Beast. Beast can retroactively study anything they have ever witnessed and keep track of the exact location of anything they have ever witnessed. In terms of Investigation, Mimir Wisdom's special ability to gain Mental Skills means the Beast has whatever skills they need (at 4+, matters for the Investigation subgame) and access to Advanced Library. They also get Postcognition, meaning they can just solve mysteries essentially at will.<br /> <br /> I don'r think there is a comparison here. Beast makes Mekhet look bad.<br /> <br /> Infiltration Vampire<br /> Disciplines: Obfuscate 3<br /> Merits: Barfly, Close Quarters Fighting 4<br /> Note: Obfuscate 1 is an infiltration add on to anyone.<br /> <br /> Comparison:<br /> The Vampire can, for free, go unnoticed. They can hide other objects or even other people. If they spend blood, they can go completely invisible, requiring an extended action to see through. Best of all? Breaking Invisibility for one person doesn't break it for other people!<br /> <br /> The Beast gets significant bonuses to amd extra excuses to use Stealth. They can become completely invisible by spending a Saity, and the invisibility only drops dor a turn when they attack. They alsp gain the ability to perfectly go incorporeal in shadows, see through shadows, and shadow teleport. You Are Not Alone, possibly with Fist of Nightmares and/or Fear is Contagious is the stealth sledgehammer, but you need to target individuals.<br /> <br /> Honestly? Advantage Vampires, here. Obfuscate just offers such an overwhelming stealth kit, and the innate ability to attack while remaining stealthed to everyone else and the power to stealth other people is just hard to compete with. Beast is slightly better at getting in to places.<br /> <br /> Combat Vampire<br /> Disciplines: Protean 3 -or- Celerity 1 + Vigor 2 or Fortitude 2<br /> Merits: Swarm Form 2 (if Protean), Combat Merits to taste (Grappling Style!)<br /> <br /> Comparison<br /> ... yeah. Beast wins. This isn't a meaningful contest. Lair Traits by itself wrecks anything a vampire can bring to the table. Swarm Form is almost as survivable as Unbreakable Beasts. Almost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T16:13:55-07:00","id":1122114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1119620-beast-analysis-cross-gaming?p=1122045#post1122045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets see...<br /> <br /> Social Beast<br /> Atavisms: Alien Allure; ???<br /> Nightmares: You Must Obey; ???<br /> Merits: Striking Looks 2, Advanced Striking Looks 2, Sympathetic 2, Fast-Talking 4<br /> <br /> Investigative / Tracking Beast<br /> Atavisms: Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must<br /> Nightmares: You Deserve This; ???<br /> Merits: Advanced Eidetic Memory 1, Direction Sense 1, Advanced Direction Sense 2, Epic Direction Sense 2, Eye for the Strange 2, ??? 2<br /> <br /> Infiltration Beast<br /> Atavisms: From the Shadows; Shadowed Soul<br /> Nightmares: You Are Not Alone; ???<br /> Merits: Close-Quarters Fighting 4, ??? 6<br /> <br /> Combat Beast<br /> ....<br /> Okay, so real talk for a minute. Literally any Beast with a damaging environmental tilt and an easily accessible tilt wins against anything not immune. You get Behold, My True Form! To help round out any of the other concepts with combat, particularly with other metaNightmares.<br /> <br /> Shadowed Soul + Behold, My True Form! / Siren's Song lets you attack from relative safety.<br /> <br /> Infested + Fist of Nightmares lets you do a lot of damage to people. Throw in Basilisk's Touch for added goodness.<br /> <br /> Looming Presence + A Good Intimidation Roll will let you one shot most people.<br /> <br /> Cyclopean Strength makes your strength based attacks automatically hit. Combine with the above.<br /> <br /> Epic Iron Skin + Unbreakable makes for a nearly unkillable juggernaut.<br /> <br /> Killer Instinct 3 + Advanced Killer Instinct 1 is a nice damaging add on.<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter + Unbreakable + Epic Iron Skin 5 + Killer Instinct 3 + Advanced Killer Instinct 1 can handle anything.<br /> <br /> Just so many options for Combat, and none of them terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you have to roll at least a success to get that though, it's not just &quot;bam everything hits&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T03:59:52-07:00","id":1122287,"title":"","content":"Tilts are actually pretty easy to inflict.Using your Dragon's Breath to turn the entire are into an inferno? You don't even need an individual target for that. You breathe fire to set things on fire, then make it an inferno, then if you have it you can do sealed portals and lock everyone in with you while it burns. Oh, and you're immune to the burning. So that's a thing. You don't even need a merit for this. You can do it at the start of the game if you want to. Start a fire, sit in the middle of it, and watch people burn alive. You'll probably even GAIN satiety off this, even if you spent it on the initial atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T06:44:29-07:00","id":1122320,"title":"","content":"As long as the heat of the fire fits your Lair trait' s fire rating, I believe. Which is not too hard: just dont take Chemical fire/ molten metal levels and you're good.<br /> <br /> Other easy to use Lair traits are poor light, fog, blazing light, downpour, slick, etc.<br /> smoke grenades, oil, flashbangs, powerbeams, natural occuring rain, emergency sprinklers, etc are transportable. Cutting the Power at night is often enough to draw Upon Poor light.<br /> Your minor traits are very important for a reason. It's mostly about manipulating your environment in clever ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}